 "subtitle": "The garden of a giant with implanted memories",
 "line": "Year 3000. You walk into the brain of Titan, a giant built to restore human feeling.",
 "synopsis": "Year 3000, after civilisation resets. You walk into the brain of Titan, a giant artificial being built to restore human feeling. Steel joints and kinetic wires at the entrance contract and expand like breath. In the central void an android head trembles its eyelids and weeps, circled by metal conifers and drifting lens shards. The visitor is not a shopper but an explorer, collecting a new visual self.",
 "keywords": [
  "Defamiliarisation",
  "Breathing machines",
  "Collecting"
 ],
 "quote": "Not a shopper. An explorer, collecting a new visual self.",
 "why": [
  {
   "t": "The entrance is a threshold",
   "d": "Two steel joints and a wire curtain stand 1-3 m inside the door; you pass through a gap before the room opens."
  },
  {
   "t": "One head, alone, at the centre",
   "d": "The android head is the only object in an 8 x 7 m void; the route circles it and never crosses it."
  },
  {
   "t": "Product sits outside the loop",
   "d": "Collecting stations sit at the outer corners; you turn away from the head to find the eyewear."
  },
  {
   "t": "Payment is the far point",
   "d": "The collection desk closes the loop at the back."
  }
 ],
